    "SourceNote": "Imported 2026-08-16 from vendor/CarveraProfiles/CAM_Post_Processors/Freecad/Tools/bit/Makera_Spiral_O_3.175_25mm_Plastic.fctb (Makera 'Spiral O 3.175*25mm', plastic preset: 1000 mm/min, 10000 RPM, stepdown 1). Feeds pulled back to ~2/3 (700 mm/min, 0.07 mm/tooth) per the Carvera Air audible-profile rule (docs/carvera-air.md) for the epoxy relief job. Single-flute up-cut O-flute: the big gullet is why it's the roughing tool for resin/epoxy - chips clear instead of re-welding. 25 mm flute = full reach for a 20 mm-deep relief with the shank never below the flute (shank = flute diameter, so no shank-rub check needed). Attribute keys translated Makera->FreeCAD PathBit (cutting_feedrate->HorizFeed, plunge_feedrate->VertFeed, ramp_feedrate->RampFeed, stepdown->Stepdown, rampAngle->RampAngle); stepover added (Makera gives none for a flat mill) at ~38% of diameter."
